A joint multi-result template whose results share an outer generic type,
(A[T], A[U]), with a single consumer A[int]. The demand A[int] unifies with both
result slots, but it pins only one: plumb instantiates Make[int, U] (lifting U),
producing A[int] for the consumer and A[U] as a lifted output. It must not pin both
parameters from the one demand (Make[int, int]), which would produce A[int] twice
and be wrongly rejected as an ambiguous producer.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type A[T any] struct{ V T }

//plumb:build
func Make[T, U any]() (A[T], A[U]) { return A[T]{}, A[U]{} }

//plumb:build
func UseInt(a A[int]) int { return 0 }
